                            <comment id="16501720" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 5 Jun 2018 12:56:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Not an issue. Authentication was introduced only in AI 2.5. Users are not expected to pass credentials before that.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16501773" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 5 Jun 2018 13:28:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ilyak&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ilyak&quot;&gt;ilyak&lt;/a&gt;, reopening, this is an issue. The problem is that we do not check authentication enabled flag in JDBC driver. The same logic implemented correctly for ODBC and thin clients.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
